# Security

This repo will handle advisory data and lockfile writes.
Treat that as sensitive automation.

- Never commit `.env`, tokens, npm tokens, GitHub PATs, or real audit dumps
- Default to dry-run for any command that would mutate `package.json`, lockfiles, git, or remotes
- Do not phone home; no telemetry
- Do not fetch advisories in tests unless fixtures are checked in
- When implementing later: pin sources, record provenance (advisory id, affected range, chosen version)
- Agent sessions must not run `npm publish`, force-push, or `git push origin`
